    {
      "id": "r20261115-a02",
      "title": "Urban Farming: Food from the City",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "In many big cities, fresh vegetables travel hundreds of kilometers before they reach your plate. Some city people are now trying a different idea: growing food where they live. This is called urban farming.",
        "Urban farms can be very small. A family might grow chilies and tomatoes in pots on a balcony. Neighbors sometimes turn an empty piece of land into a shared garden. Some companies even grow vegetables inside buildings, using special lights instead of sunlight.",
        "Urban farming brings real benefits. The food is fresh and does not need long truck rides, so it is better for the environment. Gardening is also good exercise and a way to meet neighbors. A few pots of vegetables will not feed a whole city, but they can change how people think about their food."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "reach": "mencapai",
        "balcony": "balkon",
        "empty": "kosong",
        "shared": "bersama",
        "sunlight": "sinar matahari",
        "benefits": "manfaat",
        "truck rides": "perjalanan truk",
        "exercise": "olahraga"
      },
